From 2bba20f5b271a4a8daeb2009a75f899aadf9c17b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hiper25 <whydonit@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:34:51 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] drm/meson: implement native SC2 TMDS display support

SC2 uses the HDMI 2.0 TMDS controller with separate CLKCTRL, ANACTRL
and PWRCTRL banks. TOP at fe300000 precedes DWC at fe308000, unlike
the G12A combined mapping. Implement its actual PLL lock sequences,
PHY settings and resets, firmware power domain and video SRAM gates.

Reuse the G12A OSD/VPP layout selected for SC2 by the vendor source,
not a foreign fallback compatible. Preserve full-width fractional PLL
parameters, wire canvas/HDMI endpoints and native board HPD/DDC pins.

Expose the real DW-HDMI audio codec but leave CEC disabled. No forced
EDID or board HPD/+5V manipulation is added, and this is not a TCL
picture-setting fix. Initial acceptance is 1080p60 RGB 8bpc; visible
output and audio remain subject to combined build and board testing.

Change-Id: I8eb94879a7c9f48522ed1b43a3c5ec2d5e24690a
